r76/warden`). `--histor` asks the public HISTOR log whether a server serves you what it serves everyone; for a remote server it sends the endpoint and a digest, for a stdio server started from npm or PyPI the package name (`npm:<name>`, `pypi:<name>`, which HISTOR runs in a gVisor sandbox) and a digest — never tool text.\n## Development\n\nbash Copy\n    \n    `npm install && npm run build && npm test   # 443 tests\n    `\n\n`test/packaging.test.ts` is what keeps the headline honest: it fails if an npm runtime dependency appears, if any source file imports outside the package (except `node:` builtins), or if the entry point stops exporting the enforcement surface. `test/mcp-server.test.ts` is the Glama health check: `initialize` + `tools/list` + a `tools/call`.\n\nUsed by ARGUS (the reference host), MOMUS (the publisher side), and the AICOM MCP-security course.\n\nMIT © AICOM (alexar76)\n\n## Checked by Odel\n\n  * Registry verified the namespace io.github.alexar76\n  * Repository reachable, not archived\n\n### Assessed by AI Jev\n\nHarmful\n    \n    5%\nFirst-party\n    \n    33%\nHigh impact\n    \n    9%\nAdult content\n    \n    1%\n\nRead from the listing and README on 15 Oct 2026. AI can make mistakes: a guide, not a check.\n\n## Requirements\n\nRuns\n    On your machine\n\nSign-in\n    npm\n\nCredentials\n    None asked\n\nClients\n    Any MCP client\n\n  * @aimarket/warden@0.16.0 npm 830 a week\n\n## Details\n\nVersion\n    0.16.0\n\nUpdated\n    14 Oct 2026\n\nRepo created\n    24 Aug 2026\n\nLicense\n    MIT\n\nLanguage\n    TypeScript\n\nGitHub\n    0 stars · 0 forks · 0 issues\n\nRegistry name\n    io.github.alexar76/warden\n\n  * alexar76/warden\n  * warden.modelmarket.dev\n  * Registry listing--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nalexar76 (Aleksandr Artamokhov) (https://huggingface.co/alexar76/activity/all)\nciteturn0search9 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 weeks ago; alexar76/histor-mcp-tool-definitions Viewer 